        <headline>AOG SUPPORT - TSRV SYSTEMS - RH BLEED DEFECT</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: THIS AIRCRAFT IS CURRENTLY AOG DUE TO LOW RH DUCT PRESSURE AT IDLE AFTER AN ENGINE CHANGE.
THE RH PRSOV, BAR, HSR AND HSV HAVE BEEN REPLACED.

ACTION:

1). OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2). USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.  
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.  

3). CHECK HIGH STAGE REGULATOR FOR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.

4). CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

5). LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY REF AMM TASK 36-11-00-700-802. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:
A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE.
B) CONTROL PRESSURE SENSE LINE TO PRSOV.    
C) CONTROL PRESSURE SENSE LINE FROM HSR TO HSV.
D). SUPPLY PRESSURE SENSE LINE TO HSR.

6). CHECK  DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE PN 16135-81 FOR OBSTRUCTION USING COMPRESSED NITROGEN.

7). RETURN AC TO SERVICE WITH ALL FINDINGS FROM THIS WO DOCUMENTED AND CLOSED EITHER THROUGH POSITIVE MAINTENANCE ACTION OR AN ACCEPTABLE DEFERRAL</description>
        <descriptionSign>JMON</descriptionSign>
